WEBVTT

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.727
NEAT starts with a population of two hundred random networks.

00:00:09.727 --> 00:00:15.864
Each one is described by a genome: a list of its nodes and its weighted connections.

00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:19.503
Children differ from their parents by mutation.

00:00:19.503 --> 00:00:21.934
Most mutations just change a weight.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.813
Some add a new connection.

00:00:23.813 --> 00:00:27.791
And some add a whole new node, by splitting a connection in two.

00:00:27.791 --> 00:00:30.191
That is how the networks grow.

00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:34.931
Each generation, the best fifth survive and have children.

00:00:34.931 --> 00:00:39.133
A child is a copy, or a mix of two parents, plus mutations.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.193
The two very best pass on unchanged.

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:48.636
Similar networks are grouped into species, and they mostly compete within their own species.

00:00:48.636 --> 00:00:52.967
That gives a new structure a few generations to prove itself.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.335
How good is a network?

00:00:55.335 --> 00:01:01.051
Every network walks the same three random terrains, and its fitness is the average score.

00:01:01.051 --> 00:01:05.412
The terrains change every generation, so nobody can memorise them.

00:01:05.412 --> 00:01:08.835
Later in the run, that went up to 5 terrains.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:16.192
To save time, an episode stops early if the walker makes no real progress for one hundred and fifty steps.

00:01:16.192 --> 00:01:22.300
A network that just stands there does not waste one thousand six hundred steps of compute.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.758
But this creates a trap.

00:01:24.758 --> 00:01:27.486
Standing still scores about minus nine.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:30.969
A brave attempt that falls scores minus one hundred.

00:01:30.969 --> 00:01:33.649
So at first, standing still wins.

00:01:34.249 --> 00:01:37.465
The best score in each generation is noisy.

00:01:37.465 --> 00:01:40.792
Three terrains can be lucky, or unlucky.

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:48.099
So every ten generations, the top five networks walk ten terrains they have never seen, with no early stop.

00:01:48.099 --> 00:01:50.782
The best average becomes the champion.

00:01:50.782 --> 00:01:52.531
That is the blue line.

00:01:52.531 --> 00:01:56.739
Near the end of the run, that test grew to twenty terrains.
